              "original_text": "{\"id\": \"Q118140254\", \"labels\": {\"ja\": \"日本赤十字社宮城県支部\", \"en\": \"Japanese Red Cross Society Miyagi Chapter\"}, \"descriptions\": {}}",
              "source_ref": "s8"
            },
            {
              "locator": "metadata",
              "original_text": "{\"id\": \"Q17987422\", \"labels\": {\"ja\": \"専門学校\", \"en\": \"professional training college\"}, \"descriptions\": {\"ja\": \"教育施設である専修学校のうち、専門課程を置く専修学校が称することのできる独占呼称であり、ISCED-5Bレベルに分類される高等教育機関である\", \"en\": \"vocational schools with post-secondary course in Japan\"}}",
              "source_ref": "s4"
            }
          ],
          "id": "c1",
          "value": {
            "language": "en",
            "text": "The Japanese Red Cross Ishinomaki School of Nursing (石巻赤十字看護専門学校) is a private nursing training institution in Ishinomaki, Miyagi Prefecture, Japan. It is classified as a professional training college offering a postsecondary nursing course. Wikidata identifies the Japanese Red Cross Society Miyagi Chapter as its parent organization.\n\nIts recorded founding date is 24 March 1927, when the Japanese Red Cross Society Miyagi Branch opened a relief-worker training institute. It adopted the name 石巻赤十字看護学院 in February 1948 and 石巻赤十字高等看護学院 in March 1950. On 1 April 1976, recognition as a specialized training college with a professional course under the School Education Act accompanied adoption of its present name. The nursing course received authorization to confer the specialist title in 1995.\n\nThe school offers a three-year professional nursing training course. Listed outcomes include eligibility to sit the national nursing examination, apply to public-health-nurse and midwife training institutions, and seek transfer admission to a four-year university. Following damage in the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake, school functions temporarily moved to Ishinomaki Senshu University. A new school building was completed in 2014 alongside Ishinomaki Red Cross Hospital."
          },
          "verification": "supported"
        }
